###
     ███████   ███   ███  █████████  ███████    ███  ████████   
    ███   ███  ███   ███     ███     ███   ███  ███  ███   ███  
    ███   ███  ███   ███     ███     ███   ███  ███  ███████    
    ███   ███  ███   ███     ███     ███   ███  ███  ███   ███  
     ███████    ███████      ███     ███████    ███  ███   ███  

    where -o puts a file

    the output path is the input path with the extension swapped, kept in
    the same shape. a flat input list lands flat, a nested one lands
    nested - `kode/kode/test/error.kode` has to become
    `js/kode1/test/error.js` and not `js/kode1/error.js`, or the
    bootstrap cannot build the tests it runs against itself.
###

use ../kode

▸ commonDir

    ▸ one directory is its own root

        kode.commonDir ['/r/a.kode' '/r/b.kode']  ▸ '/r'

    ▸ the shared directory, not the shared prefix

        kode.commonDir ['/r/kode/a.kode' '/r/kol/b.kode']  ▸ '/r'

    ▸ a single file is its own root

        kode.commonDir ['/r/a.kode']  ▸ '/r'

    ▸ nothing in common falls back to the filesystem root

        kode.commonDir ['/r/a.kode' '/s/b.kode']  ▸ '/'

    ▸ no files at all

        kode.commonDir []  ▸ '/'

▸ outPath

    ▸ a flat list stays flat

        kode.outPath '/r/a.kode' '/out' '/r'  ▸ '/out/a.js'

    ▸ a nested file stays nested

        kode.outPath '/r/test/b.kode' '/out' '/r'  ▸ '/out/test/b.js'

    ▸ two levels deep

        kode.outPath '/r/a/b/c.kode' '/out' '/r'  ▸ '/out/a/b/c.js'

    ▸ the extension is swapped, whatever it was

        kode.outPath '/r/test/c.noon' '/out' '/r'  ▸ '/out/test/c.js'

    ▸ a file outside the root keeps its name

        kode.outPath '/s/b.kode' '/out' '/r'  ▸ '/out/b.js'

    ▸ a file whose name starts with the root is not the root

        kode.outPath '/rb.kode' '/out' '/r'  ▸ '/out/rb.js'

▸ the root the bootstrap would pick

    ▸ the compiler and its tests share one

        kode.commonDir ['kode/kode/parse.kode' 'kode/kode/test/error.kode']  ▸ 'kode/kode'

    ▸ the compiler on its own

        kode.commonDir ['kode/kode/parse.kode' 'kode/kode/lexer.kode']  ▸ 'kode/kode'